  "body": "This gets Ash's Stripe practice run ready (checks 3\u20135). Until now, a refunded or disputed sale still read \"paid\".\n\n**What changes:**\n- **Refunds:** `charge.refunded` sets the order to partly_refunded or refunded, with the amount refunded.\n- **Disputes:** `charge.dispute.created` sets it to disputed. When the dispute closes, a win sets it back to paid and a loss sets it to dispute_lost, with the reason recorded.\n- **Finding the order:** by the payment intent the order learned when it was paid, or by its metadata for older orders.\n- **The split:** each order carries paid, Cohabi's cut, the seller's share and the amount refunded, so a seller can recompute it. The wallet's Sales list shows it.\n\nTests: stripe-checkout.mjs (7/7) and every checkout, order and sales test pass.\n\n**Operator step after deploy:** subscribe the Stripe webhook endpoint to `charge.refunded`, `charge.dispute.created` and `charge.dispute.closed` in the Stripe dashboard.\n\n**Not decided here:** COMMONS_FEE_PERCENT is 0, and on these destination charges the platform pays Stripe's card fee. That's a council and Geoffrey decision before live money.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
